    description: "CAP's Rebel, model OB-86PBCK2000, is a dedicated power bar rather than a multi-purpose one, and it fills the gap this page otherwise leaves for lifters who mainly squat, bench and deadlift. CAP describes it as its 7 ft heavy-duty power bar with a maximum capacity of 2,000 lb, and the Amazon listing gives the same 2,000 lb figure. Iron Company, a CAP retailer, lists it at 20 kg and 86 inches, with 51.5 inches between the collars, a medium diamond knurl with a center knurl, copper alloy bushings, ribbed sleeves and a black oxide finish on shaft and sleeves, and gives a 5-year warranty against defects that excludes bends from storing the bar loaded. Iron Company also lists a 190,000 PSI tensile strength and a 30 mm shaft; we did not find either on CAP's own page, so neither is on the card. The Amazon listing showed $229.99 on 9 November 2026. The trade-offs come with the type: the center knurl and thicker shaft that help a heavy squat get in the way of cleans and snatches, and black oxide needs brushing and oiling in a damp garage.",
  },
  {
    id: "synergee-regional-15kg",
    name: "Synergee Regional Olympic 15kg Women’s Barbell",
    brand: "Synergee",
    category: "15 kg bar with a 25 mm shaft",
    badge: "Best 15 kg Bar",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B072LNZR5W?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
